WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.459
Maybe there was a reason that you...

00:00:01.459 --> 00:00:04.295
[body passing gas]

00:00:04.295 --> 00:00:07.632
I have never heard

00:00:07.632 --> 00:00:10.969
a deceased body pass gas.

00:00:10.969 --> 00:00:12.637
My name is Evie Vargas,

00:00:12.637 --> 00:00:15.724
and I am a funeral director and embalmer.

00:00:15.724 --> 00:00:19.102
I have been in the funeral
industry for 10 years

00:00:19.102 --> 00:00:21.396
and wouldn't have it any other way.

00:00:21.396 --> 00:00:23.440
Today, we are going to be looking at

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:26.109
dead-body scenes in movies and TV

00:00:26.109 --> 00:00:27.944
and judge how realistic they are.

00:00:27.944 --> 00:00:30.739
One, two, three.

00:00:33.658 --> 00:00:34.659
Whoa.

00:00:34.659 --> 00:00:35.827
Angel lust.

00:00:35.827 --> 00:00:40.498
So, angel lust is a term
that I was not familiar with

00:00:40.498 --> 00:00:42.208
until I saw this clip.

00:00:42.208 --> 00:00:47.088
Angel lust is a postmortem
erection that happens to men

00:00:47.088 --> 00:00:49.674
that have been executed by hanging.

00:00:49.674 --> 00:00:52.594
I have never seen this before.

00:00:52.594 --> 00:00:55.430
Even if angel lust is real,

00:00:55.430 --> 00:00:57.140
the deceased in the clip

00:00:57.140 --> 00:01:00.685
does not seem to be deceased by hanging.

00:01:00.685 --> 00:01:03.897
I just think it's a bit disrespectful.

00:01:03.897 --> 00:01:07.776
It really wants that shock
value from the audience.

00:01:07.776 --> 00:01:08.610
Well, I'd love to,

00:01:08.610 --> 00:01:10.528
but I've got a dead
body in the car with me.

00:01:10.528 --> 00:01:12.447
Just a glass of wine. 15 minutes.

00:01:12.447 --> 00:01:14.824
The dead guy won't mind.

00:01:14.824 --> 00:01:16.242
Do me a favor, keep it out of the sun.

00:01:16.242 --> 00:01:17.285
Yeah, sure.

00:01:17.285 --> 00:01:19.204
That is not common practice,

00:01:19.204 --> 00:01:20.747
to leave a body in a car,

00:01:20.747 --> 00:01:21.956
to leave a body in a car,

00:01:21.956 --> 00:01:24.417
in the hearse, anywhere.

00:01:24.417 --> 00:01:27.337
The person that is driving the deceased

00:01:27.337 --> 00:01:29.172
is in possession of that body

00:01:29.172 --> 00:01:32.008
and is responsible for whatever happens

00:01:32.008 --> 00:01:33.885
at this point forward.

00:01:33.885 --> 00:01:36.096
This will definitely get on the news,

00:01:36.096 --> 00:01:37.931
and you can ruin your business.

00:01:37.931 --> 00:01:41.017
Usually it's just a regular van.

00:01:41.017 --> 00:01:43.478
There's no refrigeration.

00:01:43.478 --> 00:01:46.147
[body gurgling]

00:01:47.190 --> 00:01:49.776
They make these noises. The air comes out.

00:01:49.776 --> 00:01:52.779
It's like [growling].

00:01:52.779 --> 00:01:55.240
So, I have heard that noise,

00:01:55.240 --> 00:02:00.036
but it's not consistent
to how it actually sounds.

00:02:00.036 --> 00:02:02.330
It's more of like a growling.

00:02:02.330 --> 00:02:06.668
It's just air passing
through the vocal chords.

00:02:06.668 --> 00:02:08.211
It doesn't last long.

00:02:08.211 --> 00:02:11.714
It will scare you when it does happen.

00:02:11.714 --> 00:02:12.715
[growling]

00:02:12.715 --> 00:02:16.386
Nate's imitation is actually accurate

00:02:16.386 --> 00:02:18.680
to how it actually sounds in real life.

00:02:22.809 --> 00:02:24.686
The table that Nate is on

00:02:24.686 --> 00:02:26.855
is a porcelain embalming table.

00:02:26.855 --> 00:02:29.649
That is where the embalming
process takes place.

00:02:29.649 --> 00:02:32.610
There is running water
constantly running on the table.

00:02:32.610 --> 00:02:34.279
That drain allows for the water,

00:02:34.279 --> 00:02:38.408
blood, and other fluid
to drain into the sewer.

00:02:38.408 --> 00:02:40.243
What I find to be unrealistic

00:02:40.243 --> 00:02:42.996
is that he is not wearing gloves.

00:02:42.996 --> 00:02:46.958
Doesn't have a disposable
mask on, or even a shield.

00:02:46.958 --> 00:02:50.044
You have to treat every decedent

00:02:50.044 --> 00:02:52.672
as if they are contagious

00:02:52.672 --> 00:02:55.341
and use personal protective equipment.

00:02:55.341 --> 00:02:58.845
I would rate this scene 3 out of 10,

00:02:58.845 --> 00:03:00.847
just because he left the body.

00:03:00.847 --> 00:03:02.098
You don't do that.

00:03:02.098 --> 00:03:03.725
Chris: Holy s---, look at that!

00:03:03.725 --> 00:03:04.559
Georgie: What?

00:03:04.559 --> 00:03:07.103
Chris: He was clean-shaven.
He's got a f---ing beard now.

00:03:07.103 --> 00:03:10.815
It looks like the deceased
is wrapped in plastic.

00:03:10.815 --> 00:03:14.152
But this also looks like

00:03:14.152 --> 00:03:15.945
it can be skin slip,

00:03:15.945 --> 00:03:20.408
where the skin slips off of the body.

00:03:20.408 --> 00:03:24.204
The eyes are not consistent
with decomposed body.

00:03:24.204 --> 00:03:28.750
When someone dies, the pressure
in their eyes will decrease.

00:03:28.750 --> 00:03:31.336
The color of the eye would become cloudy.

00:03:31.336 --> 00:03:33.630
Oh, look at his fingernails!

00:03:33.630 --> 00:03:36.674
It is a common misconception that hair

00:03:36.674 --> 00:03:39.427
and nails continue to grow.

00:03:39.427 --> 00:03:43.348
Skin becomes dehydrated
and gives the illusion

00:03:43.348 --> 00:03:46.434
that the hair is longer and
that the nails are longer

00:03:46.434 --> 00:03:50.271
when in fact it's just the skin shrinking.

00:03:50.271 --> 00:03:53.942
This actually looks like degloving.

00:03:53.942 --> 00:03:58.321
That happens where the
entire skin of the hand

00:03:58.321 --> 00:04:00.823
just peels off.

00:04:00.823 --> 00:04:04.744
Water would accelerate decomposition.

00:04:04.744 --> 00:04:08.957
And the body doesn't look like
it was submerged in water.

00:04:08.957 --> 00:04:13.002
You would not be able
to identify the remains.

00:04:13.002 --> 00:04:16.256
It would be bloated.

00:04:16.256 --> 00:04:19.759
And it just depends how long
the person was in the water.

00:04:19.759 --> 00:04:21.719
I'm gonna f---ing puke!

00:04:21.719 --> 00:04:24.847
It can be a strong smell
for certain people.

00:04:24.847 --> 00:04:27.767
They can't handle the
smell of decomposition.

00:04:27.767 --> 00:04:30.687
I use a respirator where
you can barely smell.

00:04:30.687 --> 00:04:33.064
But sometimes it's so
strong that even that,

00:04:33.064 --> 00:04:35.858
it's, like, it's very overpowering.

00:04:35.858 --> 00:04:40.196
The deceased in this clip
does not look real at all.

00:04:40.196 --> 00:04:43.825
I would rate this clip a 2 out of 10.

00:04:43.825 --> 00:04:45.618
Yes, yes, I knew it!

00:04:45.618 --> 00:04:47.704
Thank you, Bernie, thank you!

00:04:47.704 --> 00:04:50.999
Some bodies experience rigor mortis.

00:04:50.999 --> 00:04:53.793
He doesn't seem to be experiencing that.

00:04:53.793 --> 00:04:56.045
Rigor mortis is the stiffening of joints

00:04:56.045 --> 00:04:59.882
and muscles within the
deceased human body.

00:04:59.882 --> 00:05:03.094
His body seems to be very pliable.

00:05:03.094 --> 00:05:06.681
What I'm thinking is, just
to try to justify this scene,

00:05:06.681 --> 00:05:11.519
is they are unknowingly
breaking the rigor.

00:05:11.519 --> 00:05:14.230
Breaking the rigor isn't necessarily

00:05:14.230 --> 00:05:17.317
breaking bones or breaking anything,

00:05:17.317 --> 00:05:21.279
it's just flexing the
arms, flexing the legs,

00:05:21.279 --> 00:05:24.490
flexing the head, and loosening it up

00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:26.409
where you can move the body

00:05:26.409 --> 00:05:29.787
in any way that the embalmer wants.

00:05:29.787 --> 00:05:32.123
Who's your boss? Come on, let's go.

00:05:32.123 --> 00:05:32.957
Whoa!

00:05:33.833 --> 00:05:35.418
They're moving him so much.

00:05:35.418 --> 00:05:38.963
If he has contents in his
stomach, they may come up.

00:05:38.963 --> 00:05:40.423
5 out of 10.

00:05:40.423 --> 00:05:43.343
Just because he is dead

00:05:43.343 --> 00:05:46.095
does not mean he will
necessarily lose color.

00:05:46.095 --> 00:05:48.514
It just depends on his cause of death

00:05:48.514 --> 00:05:50.767
and other environmental factors.

00:05:55.646 --> 00:05:57.732
I do not cut the clothes.

00:05:57.732 --> 00:06:00.151
The family more than likely

00:06:00.151 --> 00:06:03.196
wants those articles of clothing back.

00:06:05.448 --> 00:06:09.869
The embalmer in this
scene is utilizing wax

00:06:09.869 --> 00:06:12.163
with a spatula, which is consistent.

00:06:12.163 --> 00:06:15.416
So, to fill in that
area of missing tissue,

00:06:15.416 --> 00:06:18.211
you would want to build
up that area with wax

00:06:18.211 --> 00:06:19.962
and then cosmetize over it.

00:06:21.047 --> 00:06:22.006
Eliot: His mouth.

00:06:22.006 --> 00:06:26.969
That is an S-curve needle and wax ligature

00:06:26.969 --> 00:06:29.847
that I use in the embalming room.

00:06:32.475 --> 00:06:35.686
This is exactly how I would do it.

00:06:35.686 --> 00:06:38.856
What he is about to do is
suture the mouth closed,

00:06:38.856 --> 00:06:42.568
and he is utilizing

00:06:42.568 --> 00:06:44.529
the muscular suture.

00:06:44.529 --> 00:06:48.074
There isn't necessarily
a sound that happens

00:06:48.074 --> 00:06:50.701
when you suture the mouth closed,

00:06:50.701 --> 00:06:53.913
so I think this is just a bit exaggerated.

00:06:53.913 --> 00:06:58.543
He does tie the suture in a knot.

00:06:58.543 --> 00:07:00.795
I do a bow.

00:07:00.795 --> 00:07:01.754
Now the eyes.

00:07:04.632 --> 00:07:06.801
And those are eye caps.

00:07:06.801 --> 00:07:09.262
To make sure that

00:07:09.262 --> 00:07:12.473
the eye is set in place,

00:07:12.473 --> 00:07:16.853
it does have ridges on the
top to grip the eyelid.

00:07:16.853 --> 00:07:19.897
You would not be able to see this at all.

00:07:19.897 --> 00:07:21.441
You wouldn't even know that someone

00:07:21.441 --> 00:07:23.860
has this under their eyelids.

00:07:23.860 --> 00:07:27.363
Sometimes we do put a massage cream

00:07:27.363 --> 00:07:30.491
to make sure that the
eye does not dehydrate.

00:07:30.491 --> 00:07:33.661
I would rate this scene a

00:07:33.661 --> 00:07:34.704
8 out of 10.

00:07:34.704 --> 00:07:37.665
The only inconsistency I find

00:07:37.665 --> 00:07:42.628
is the order in which
he is closing the mouth

00:07:42.628 --> 00:07:45.173
and putting in the eye caps.

00:07:47.133 --> 00:07:49.051
No, don't! [gasps]

00:07:50.219 --> 00:07:52.680
So, each body would be placed

00:07:52.680 --> 00:07:55.308
in their own body bag.

00:07:55.308 --> 00:07:57.185
I've never seen a clear body bag.

00:07:57.185 --> 00:08:02.190
The bag would probably be black, white.

00:08:02.356 --> 00:08:04.525
It's not a see-through bag at all.

00:08:04.525 --> 00:08:08.779
Bodies are transported from
hospitals, from people's homes.

00:08:08.779 --> 00:08:11.032
There needs to be some discretion there.

00:08:11.032 --> 00:08:12.909
Madison: Nice legs over here.

00:08:12.909 --> 00:08:14.869
A great set of guns.

00:08:14.869 --> 00:08:17.330
The way the bodies are just

00:08:17.330 --> 00:08:20.500
kind of just laying
there and thrown there,

00:08:20.500 --> 00:08:23.794
there is a lot more respect and dignity

00:08:23.794 --> 00:08:27.381
that goes into placing
the dismembered bodies

00:08:27.381 --> 00:08:28.674
into the body bags.

00:08:28.674 --> 00:08:32.345
They definitely would not
be piled in that manner.

00:08:33.262 --> 00:08:35.097
We take the best boy parts,

00:08:35.097 --> 00:08:37.433
we attach them to Kyle's head,

00:08:37.433 --> 00:08:40.102
and we build the perfect boyfriend.

00:08:40.102 --> 00:08:42.813
I find that a lot of movies

00:08:42.813 --> 00:08:46.692
want to imitate livor mortis,

00:08:46.692 --> 00:08:51.405
which is the purplish-bluish-reddish color

00:08:51.405 --> 00:08:55.243
that the skin turns when blood pools

00:08:55.243 --> 00:08:57.370
to the dependent parts of the body.

00:08:57.370 --> 00:09:00.456
So when a body is laying down,

00:09:00.456 --> 00:09:02.959
the blood would pool to
the back of the head,

00:09:02.959 --> 00:09:05.503
leaving that skin color.

00:09:05.503 --> 00:09:08.047
So a lot of movies like
to show that bluish color

00:09:08.047 --> 00:09:11.801
to show the audience that,
OK, this person is dead.

00:09:11.801 --> 00:09:13.678
And they're like, "All right, we know."

00:09:13.678 --> 00:09:17.348
That's not the case for every
person that dies, though.

00:09:17.348 --> 00:09:21.811
Not every person turns that
bluish color, reddish color.

00:09:21.811 --> 00:09:24.772
I would rate this scene a 1 out of 10.

00:09:24.772 --> 00:09:26.566
There are cameras.

00:09:26.566 --> 00:09:28.442
There is security.

00:09:28.442 --> 00:09:30.152
Bodies are not unattended.

00:09:32.488 --> 00:09:35.491
Then maybe, just maybe there
was a reason that you ...

00:09:35.491 --> 00:09:38.369
[body passing gas]

00:09:38.369 --> 00:09:41.664
I have never heard

00:09:41.664 --> 00:09:45.167
a deceased body pass gas.

00:09:45.167 --> 00:09:47.837
I know that the stomach

00:09:47.837 --> 00:09:51.841
can accumulate a lot of
gas and will distend.

00:09:51.841 --> 00:09:54.468
Gas can accumulate in the abdomen,

00:09:54.468 --> 00:09:56.304
and it is relieved

00:09:56.304 --> 00:09:59.765
by suctioning out, or aspirating,

00:09:59.765 --> 00:10:02.977
the abdominal and chest cavities.

00:10:02.977 --> 00:10:06.022
Once you aspirate and use the trocar

00:10:06.022 --> 00:10:08.107
to alleviate all of that gas

00:10:08.107 --> 00:10:09.275
so it has somewhere to go.

00:10:09.275 --> 00:10:11.485
I can't say for every single body

00:10:11.485 --> 00:10:14.947
that they accumulate
gas in their stomachs,

00:10:14.947 --> 00:10:17.908
but some do.

00:10:17.908 --> 00:10:21.329
So, I don't know how long
he's been in the water.

00:10:21.329 --> 00:10:23.831
I would assume several days.

00:10:23.831 --> 00:10:25.333
If that's true,

00:10:25.333 --> 00:10:27.001
this body is not consistent

00:10:27.001 --> 00:10:29.837
with a person that has been in the water

00:10:29.837 --> 00:10:31.464
for several days.

00:10:31.464 --> 00:10:33.799
It would not be a sight to see.

00:10:33.799 --> 00:10:37.178
A bloated body would look

00:10:37.178 --> 00:10:38.638
several times larger

00:10:38.638 --> 00:10:41.432
than its actual size.

00:10:41.432 --> 00:10:45.186
The features may look distorted

00:10:45.186 --> 00:10:49.231
and not be easily identifiable.

00:10:49.231 --> 00:10:50.483
You may have skin.

00:10:50.483 --> 00:10:52.026
It just all depends.

00:10:52.026 --> 00:10:54.654
It's the temperature of the water,

00:10:54.654 --> 00:10:56.238
how long you've been in the water,

00:10:56.238 --> 00:10:58.699
how advanced decomposition.

00:10:58.699 --> 00:11:00.993
Did this person drown or not?

00:11:00.993 --> 00:11:02.745
Were they thrown in the water?

00:11:02.745 --> 00:11:05.831
So I would find that to be unrealistic.

00:11:05.831 --> 00:11:08.417
The way the body looks,

00:11:08.417 --> 00:11:10.878
I'm assuming that he has been in the water

00:11:10.878 --> 00:11:12.046
for several days,

00:11:12.046 --> 00:11:16.676
and I just don't find that it's realistic

00:11:16.676 --> 00:11:20.054
and it's decomposed enough to be true.

00:11:20.054 --> 00:11:23.140
I would rate this scene a

00:11:23.140 --> 00:11:24.517
1 out of 10.

00:11:25.810 --> 00:11:27.436
Zelda: Ah, that's very nice.

00:11:28.604 --> 00:11:33.526
The makeup in this scene
is vibrant. It pops.

00:11:33.526 --> 00:11:35.361
It's not necessarily

00:11:35.361 --> 00:11:38.989
what families want to see

00:11:38.989 --> 00:11:42.159
when they are viewing their loved one.

00:11:42.159 --> 00:11:45.871
Usually when a family comes
into the funeral home,

00:11:45.871 --> 00:11:47.832
they provide a photo.

00:11:47.832 --> 00:11:52.378
I try to get as close to
that photo as possible.

00:11:52.378 --> 00:11:55.881
Leave my judgments and
my preference out of it.

00:11:57.675 --> 00:11:58.676
Zelda: What's this?

00:11:58.676 --> 00:12:00.761
The eyes tend to open up

00:12:00.761 --> 00:12:04.390
because the person does
not have the ability

00:12:04.390 --> 00:12:06.183
to keep their eyes closed anymore.

00:12:06.183 --> 00:12:08.811
Also, if the eyelid dehydrates a bit

00:12:08.811 --> 00:12:13.482
it can retract and not
come together fully.

00:12:13.482 --> 00:12:17.153
The makeup in this scene

00:12:17.153 --> 00:12:19.822
is consistent with mortuary makeup.

00:12:19.822 --> 00:12:23.784
I do have several of these
pots at the funeral home.

00:12:23.784 --> 00:12:28.497
It relies on the cold skin to blend,

00:12:28.497 --> 00:12:31.208
unlike drugstore makeup that relies on

00:12:31.208 --> 00:12:33.502
the warmth of the skin to blend evenly.

00:12:33.502 --> 00:12:36.714
I also use this palette.

00:12:36.714 --> 00:12:39.842
It basically has all the
colors that you can mix.

00:12:39.842 --> 00:12:41.969
You can make it lighter,
you can make it darker.

00:12:41.969 --> 00:12:45.264
I'll put a piece of plastic barrier

00:12:45.264 --> 00:12:48.726
so that none of the cosmetics
gets on the clothes.

00:12:48.726 --> 00:12:51.520
You two could've been the king
and queen of the golf club,

00:12:51.520 --> 00:12:52.563
so you could.

00:12:52.563 --> 00:12:54.982
The talking to the deceased,

00:12:54.982 --> 00:12:57.777
I kind of do that
sometimes when I need help

00:12:57.777 --> 00:12:59.111
or I'm struggling with something,

00:12:59.111 --> 00:13:01.030
I'm like, "Come on, help me out here."

00:13:01.030 --> 00:13:03.032
So I feel like that's very common.

00:13:04.658 --> 00:13:06.619
Zelda: Oh, good grief.

00:13:06.619 --> 00:13:10.331
I have never seen a
person come back to life.

00:13:10.331 --> 00:13:13.501
Last year, this 20-year-old woman

00:13:13.501 --> 00:13:16.337
was pronounced dead by paramedics.

00:13:16.337 --> 00:13:19.256
The embalmer was getting ready

00:13:19.256 --> 00:13:22.510
to embalm her.

00:13:22.510 --> 00:13:24.845
And when he unzipped the body bag,

00:13:24.845 --> 00:13:26.555
he saw that her eyes were open

00:13:26.555 --> 00:13:28.224
and she was still breathing.

00:13:28.224 --> 00:13:32.019
I don't think a lot of people
know that as an embalmer,

00:13:32.019 --> 00:13:33.312
we still have a duty

00:13:33.312 --> 00:13:36.899
to make sure that the deceased is dead.

00:13:36.899 --> 00:13:38.818
So we check for a pulse,

00:13:38.818 --> 00:13:40.611
check if the person's breathing,

00:13:40.611 --> 00:13:43.489
and then we go about
the embalming process.

00:13:46.617 --> 00:13:48.619
If I were to cut off a head,

00:13:48.619 --> 00:13:51.288
dust would not come out of the neck.

00:13:51.288 --> 00:13:54.291
If it was after embalming and I did this,

00:13:54.291 --> 00:13:58.045
embalming fluid may come
out of the arteries.

00:13:58.045 --> 00:14:01.173
I never really thought of that before.

00:14:01.173 --> 00:14:02.925
A 4 out of 10.

00:14:02.925 --> 00:14:05.427
Man: Stage of the embalming process.

00:14:06.887 --> 00:14:08.764
Those suspended jars in the room

00:14:08.764 --> 00:14:12.893
are gravity injector bottles or flasks.

00:14:12.893 --> 00:14:16.105
This is early embalming techniques

00:14:16.105 --> 00:14:18.774
and can actually still be used today.

00:14:18.774 --> 00:14:21.110
It just is a longer process,

00:14:21.110 --> 00:14:24.697
because they depend on gravity

00:14:24.697 --> 00:14:27.783
to inject the fluid throughout the body.

00:14:32.204 --> 00:14:35.875
Inside of the abdomen is a trocar,

00:14:35.875 --> 00:14:40.588
and that is used today
to suction out liquids

00:14:40.588 --> 00:14:44.717
from the chest cavity
and the abdominal cavity.

00:14:44.717 --> 00:14:48.262
It is also used to inject
preservative fluid,

00:14:48.262 --> 00:14:50.139
preservative cavity fluid.

00:14:54.018 --> 00:14:56.270
The clothing is removed.

00:14:56.270 --> 00:15:00.524
Towels are used to
cover the private areas.

00:15:00.524 --> 00:15:02.902
Because we do have to assess the body

00:15:02.902 --> 00:15:06.906
and make sure there aren't any incisions.

00:15:06.906 --> 00:15:09.366
The body is examined from head to toe.

00:15:09.366 --> 00:15:12.995
We try to still give respect to the body

00:15:12.995 --> 00:15:14.622
and cover those areas.

00:15:14.622 --> 00:15:18.751
Embalming the deceased where they died,

00:15:18.751 --> 00:15:20.836
like this man on his bed,

00:15:20.836 --> 00:15:24.423
is consistent with those times.

00:15:24.423 --> 00:15:28.510
I rate this scene a 9 out of 10.

00:15:28.510 --> 00:15:31.138
I find this scene to be very close

00:15:31.138 --> 00:15:33.557
to early embalming techniques.

00:15:37.353 --> 00:15:39.563
This is consistent with what I would do.

00:15:39.563 --> 00:15:43.901
I do the hair when the
deceased is in the casket.

00:15:43.901 --> 00:15:45.194
At this point,

00:15:45.194 --> 00:15:48.614
the body has been disinfected,
has been embalmed.

00:15:48.614 --> 00:15:50.407
She isn't using gloves,

00:15:50.407 --> 00:15:52.451
and I don't use gloves

00:15:52.451 --> 00:15:56.121
when I am styling hair.

00:15:56.121 --> 00:15:58.415
The rubber in the gloves just,

00:15:58.415 --> 00:16:01.460
it doesn't give me

00:16:01.460 --> 00:16:03.504
the control over the hair that I want.

00:16:04.588 --> 00:16:07.007
In movies they always say that they

00:16:07.007 --> 00:16:09.593
look like they're sleeping.

00:16:09.593 --> 00:16:11.428
She doesn't look like she's sleeping.

00:16:11.428 --> 00:16:12.680
She looks dead.

00:16:12.680 --> 00:16:16.058
My goal personally is to make them look

00:16:16.058 --> 00:16:17.351
like they are sleeping

00:16:17.351 --> 00:16:19.478
because that gives the family

00:16:19.478 --> 00:16:22.064
that peace of mind that they are OK

00:16:22.064 --> 00:16:24.733
and they don't have to worry about them.

00:16:26.735 --> 00:16:28.028
[casket crashes]

00:16:29.279 --> 00:16:32.157
The casket should be
sturdy on the church truck,

00:16:32.157 --> 00:16:35.577
which is basically a cart
that transports the casket.

00:16:35.577 --> 00:16:38.664
If the body falls in that manner

00:16:38.664 --> 00:16:40.958
and the head moves

00:16:40.958 --> 00:16:43.293
and kind of grazes against the pillow

00:16:43.293 --> 00:16:45.838
or the side of the casket,

00:16:45.838 --> 00:16:47.756
the makeup can rub off.

00:16:47.756 --> 00:16:49.925
It would have to be reapplied.

00:16:49.925 --> 00:16:53.512
So, as an embalmer,
embalmers can embalm a body

00:16:53.512 --> 00:16:56.557
to be firm, very firm,

00:16:56.557 --> 00:16:59.351
or to be more pliable.

00:16:59.351 --> 00:17:02.312
It just depends on the
funeral home, their style,

00:17:02.312 --> 00:17:04.773
how they want to present the body.

00:17:04.773 --> 00:17:07.484
A casket falling in
the manner that it fell

00:17:07.484 --> 00:17:11.238
and the way the body
moved seems to be real.

00:17:11.238 --> 00:17:13.699
Personally, that has never happened to me.

00:17:13.699 --> 00:17:16.243
My favorite movie that involves

00:17:16.243 --> 00:17:19.204
the funeral industry is "My Girl."

00:17:19.204 --> 00:17:23.417
I saw the movie 
when I was 6 years old,

00:17:23.417 --> 00:17:27.421
and since that 
age I always knew

00:17:27.421 --> 00:17:29.214
I wanted to be 
a funeral director.

